    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d756">

                <pb facs="0673" n="663" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg663"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/1–2249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-01-26T12:00:00-05:00">January 26,
                            1949—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>95. In making recommendations contained (2) your 187 Jan 22 have you taken into
                    consideration repercussions particularly on Amer community Shanghai which would
                    result therefrom? You will recall (penultimate sentence para 1 Deptel 1691 Nov
                    23 and ultimate para <pb facs="0674" n="664" xml:id="pg664"/> Deptel 2078 Dec
                        2<anchor n="22" xml:id="d756-f1"/>) that it has been made clear both in this
                    country and in China that this Govt intended maintain at full strength its
                    diplomatic and consular representation in China and that in any unforeseen
                    evacuation <hi rendition="#italic">in extremis</hi> US business and missionary
                    personnel would be accorded same facilities as official personnel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
